## 2. List Unique Cuisines in Indiranagar and Count Restaurants

In many Zomato datasets, multiple cuisines are stored in one comma-separated column. The following MySQL 8+ query separates them and counts the restaurants offering each cuisine.

**SQL Query:**

```sql
WITH RECURSIVE cuisine_split AS (
    SELECT
        name,
        TRIM(SUBSTRING_INDEX(cuisines, ',', 1)) AS cuisine,
        CASE
            WHEN cuisines LIKE '%,%'
            THEN SUBSTRING(cuisines,
                           LENGTH(SUBSTRING_INDEX(cuisines, ',', 1)) + 2)
            ELSE ''
        END AS remaining
    FROM zomato
    WHERE location = 'Indiranagar'
      AND cuisines IS NOT NULL

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        name,
        TRIM(SUBSTRING_INDEX(remaining, ',', 1)),
        CASE
            WHEN remaining LIKE '%,%'
            THEN SUBSTRING(remaining,
                           LENGTH(SUBSTRING_INDEX(remaining, ',', 1)) + 2)
            ELSE ''
        END
    FROM cuisine_split
    WHERE remaining <> ''
)
SELECT
    cuisine,
    COUNT(DISTINCT name) AS restaurant_count
FROM cuisine_split
WHERE cuisine <> ''
GROUP BY cuisine
ORDER BY restaurant_count DESC, cuisine ASC;
```

**Explanation:** The recursive CTE splits the comma-separated cuisine list into individual cuisines. The final query counts distinct restaurant names for each cuisine in Indiranagar.

**Expected output columns:**

| cuisine | restaurant_count |
|---|---:|
| North Indian | 35 |
| Chinese | 28 |
| South Indian | 21 |
| Italian | 12 |
| Continental | 10 |

